{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport bisect\n\nn, m = map(int, input().split())\na = [int(x) for x in input().split()]\nhalf = n // 2 + n % 2\notv = 0\n\ndef gen(pos, cnt):\n    out = []\n    mask = 0\n    limit = 1 << cnt\n    while mask < limit:\n        x = mask\n        s = 0\n        bit = 0\n        while bit < 20:\n            if x & 1:\n                s += a[pos + bit]\n            x >>= 1\n            bit += 1\n        out.append(s % m)\n        mask += 1\n    return out\n\nb = gen(0, half)\nb.sort()\n\nsecond_limit = 1 << (n // 2)\nmask = 0\nwhile mask < second_limit:\n    x = mask\n    t = 0\n    bit = 0\n    while bit < 20:\n        if x & 1:\n            t += a[half + bit]\n        x >>= 1\n        bit += 1\n    t %= m\n    target = m - t - 1\n    k = bisect.bisect_left(b, target)\n    if k < len(b):\n        t2 = b[k]\n        if t2 > target:\n            if k - 1 >= 0:\n                t2 = b[k - 1]\n    else:\n        t2 = b[-1]\n    otv = max(otv, (t + t2) % m, (t + b[-1]) % m)\n    mask += 1\n\nprint(otv % m)\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <cmath>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    int n, m;\n    cin >> n >> m;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        cin >> a[i];\n    }\n\n    int half = n / 2 + n % 2; // ceil(n/2)\n\n    // Generate all subset sums for first half\n    vector<int> b;\n    int cnt1 = half;\n    int limit1 = 1 << cnt1;\n    for (int mask = 0; mask < limit1; ++mask) {\n        long long sum = 0;\n        for (int bit = 0; bit < cnt1; ++bit) {\n            if (mask & (1 << bit)) {\n                sum += a[bit];\n            }\n        }\n        b.push_back(sum % m);\n    }\n    sort(b.begin(), b.end());\n\n    int second_half = n - half;\n    int limit2 = 1 << second_half;\n    int otv = 0;\n\n    for (int mask = 0; mask < limit2; ++mask) {\n        long long sum = 0;\n        for (int bit = 0; bit < second_half; ++bit) {\n            if (mask & (1 << bit)) {\n                sum += a[half + bit];\n            }\n        }\n        int t = sum % m;\n        int target = m - t - 1;\n        // Find largest b[j] such that b[j] <= target\n        auto it = lower_bound(b.begin(), b.end(), target);\n        int t2;\n        if (it == b.end()) {\n            t2 = b.back();\n        } else {\n            if (*it > target) {\n                if (it != b.begin()) {\n                    --it;\n                    t2 = *it;\n                } else {\n                    t2 = *it; // but *it > target, so t2 > target, but then t+t2 >= m? Actually if it == b.begin() and *it > target, then all b > target, so best is b[0]? But then (t+b[0])%m = t+b[0]-m? Wait, the original code: if k < len(b): t2 = b[k]; if t2 > target: if k-1>=0: t2 = b[k-1]; else: t2 = b[-1]. So if k==0 and b[0]>target, then t2 = b[-1] (last). So we need to handle that. Let's replicate exactly.\n                }\n            } else {\n                t2 = *it;\n            }\n        }\n        // Actually the original logic is more complex. Let's replicate exactly:\n        // k = bisect_left(b, target)\n        // if k < len(b):\n        //     t2 = b[k]\n        //     if t2 > target:\n        //         if k-1 >= 0: t2 = b[k-1]\n        // else:\n        //     t2 = b[-1]\n        // So we need to implement that.\n        // We'll do:\n        int k = lower_bound(b.begin(), b.end(), target) - b.begin();\n        int t2_val;\n        if (k < (int)b.size()) {\n            t2_val = b[k];\n            if (t2_val > target) {\n                if (k - 1 >= 0) {\n                    t2_val = b[k - 1];\n                }\n            }\n        } else {\n            t2_val = b.back();\n        }\n        // Then compute candidates\n        int cand1 = (t + t2_val) % m;\n        int cand2 = (t + b.back()) % m;\n        otv = max(otv, max(cand1, cand2));\n    }\n\n    cout << otv % m << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-1.4305104514278355e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0002205128694185987, -8.082063141046092e-05, -2.50339189733495e-06, -0.062307506799697876, -2.753696753643453e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -3.969590397900902e-05, -6.318072337307967e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -3.099436753473128e-06, -0.014421164989471436, -0.011051279492676258, 0.0, -0.4903806447982788, -0.49269938468933105, -0.0025336805265396833, -1.9073468138230965e-06, 0.0, -2.50339189733495e-06, -0.4771133065223694, -0.03889428824186325, -1.5616295058862306e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -4.6132929128361866e-05, -0.04870598763227463, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.1709168979432434e-05, -5.960446742392378e-06, -5.006777428206988e-06, 0.0, -1.7404405298293568e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -0.005961257498711348, -0.0019286142196506262, -3.576278118089249e-07, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -0.00012599628826137632, -2.384